  "notes": {
    "_": "This file records WHICH GATE guards each entry of the authorization surface, not whether that gate is correct. It exists because the same question -- may this actor do this? -- is answered by more than twenty distinct idiom combinations in this repository, two of which (gated-lookup, ensure-helper) are indistinguishable from an ungated method in a diff. A NEW entry, or an entry whose gate disappears, blocks; confirming the gate and running --update is the deliberate look this check is asking for.",
    "gate:NONE": "No named gate found. For most of these that is correct -- an avatar acting on its own avatar (dance, typing, posture, expression, sign, look-to) needs no authority beyond being in the room, which the avatar lookup already establishes. It is NOT automatically correct for anything that touches another player's property, currency, or the room's own settings. A new NONE is the one to read twice.",
    "gate:gated-lookup": "The gate is inside a lookup: FindManipulableItemAsync(ctx, id) asks SecurityModule.CanManipulateFurniAsync and returns null when refused. It reads like _state.ItemsById.TryGetValue(id, out item), which asks nothing. One identifier apart, opposite meaning.",
    "gate:ensure-helper": "A private static that throws -- EnsurePetOwner(ctx, pet) raises NoPermissionToManipulatePet. No return value, so nothing at the call site says a check happened.",
    "gate:IMPL-NOT-FOUND": "The declared method's implementation was not resolved by name. Not a finding on its own -- it means this check cannot speak for that entry, which is worth knowing.",
    "grain:IRoomFurni.Edit.cs::ApplyFurniEditAsync": "Deliberately gateless, and the file says so: 'the authorization question is answered once, by the caller, against room.furni.edit'. That contradicts ROOMG-GATE-038, stated in RoomSecurityModule, RoomGrain.Moderation and RoomGrain.Settings: 'a handler is not a security boundary... the grain is the one that decides'. Its one caller today (VortexApplyFurniEditMessageHandler) does check the capability. Nothing makes the next one.",
    "http:anonymous": "/api/login, /api/logout and the asset routes are anonymous by design. /api/public/* is the public surface and is not listed as anonymous because it declares no gate at all -- which is the same thing, said less clearly."
  }
}
